s at most\n\n\\[\n\\Bigl(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-1\\Bigr)+k < \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}=|T_n|.\n\\]\n\nThus the covering condition cannot be fulfilled when \\(k\\ge1\\).\n\nWhen \\(k=0\\) we keep **all** diagonals \\(d_c\\) (\\(c=2,\\dots ,n+1\\)). By Lemma\u202f1 they cover every point of \\(T_n\\), and none of the lines is sunny. Hence \\(k=0\\) is feasible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nThe only non\u2011negative integer \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two stated conditions is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}.\n\\]"
